# Production forward-only lock (from 2026-10-22)

Baseline: see `docs/PRODUCTION_FORWARD_BASELINE.md` (SHA `a0f295e9` — FMS dual videos + Field Executive Management Systems).

## Hard rules

1. **Forward only.** Production aliases on **sheetomatic-redesign** may only point at deploys whose git commit is a **descendant** of the baseline (or the baseline).
2. **Never Instant Rollback** / promote / `vercel alias set` to an older deploy behind the baseline — even if a newer build failed.
3. **Never** attach `sheetomatic.com`, `app`, `workspace`, `ai` to `sheetomatic-redesign-deploy-v2`.
4. After every production Ready: run **`npm run deploy:lock`** (`deploy:pin` then `deploy:verify`). Ship is not done until exit 0.
5. **`deploy:pin` is mandatory** — Vercel Instant Rollback / competing Production deploys have repeatedly reassigned `workspace.sheetomatic.com` to old Ready builds (e.g. `dpl_BkXikNDc`). Pinning after Ready is what keeps traffic on the tip.
6. If tip build fails (e.g. Prisma P3009): fix migrate / tip, redeploy **newer** Ready — do not leave traffic on pre-baseline aliases. Never click Instant Rollback in the Vercel UI.
7. Ignore `sheetomatic-redesign-deploy-v2` green checks — it is not the customer-domain project.

## Legacy paths removed / locked

- `/services/hr/field-tracking` → permanent redirect to `/services/field-tracking`
- Unused old `service-detail-content.tsx` removed — FMS videos live only in `services-category-content.tsx`
- Marketing smoke: `.cursor/rules/marketing-deploy-smoke.mdc`

## Advancing the lock

Only when the team lead says to advance the baseline: update `docs/PRODUCTION_FORWARD_BASELINE.md` to the new tip SHA after `deploy:verify` passes.
